sequenceDiagram
    participant P as Patient
    participant API as API Server
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant Q as BullMQ Worker
    participant GW as MockPaymentGateway

    Note over P,GW: Happy Path — Booking to Completion

    P->>API: GET /v1/doctors?specialty=Cardiology
    API->>DB: SELECT w/ indexed filters
    DB-->>API: doctor list
    API-->>P: {data: [...], total, page}

    P->>API: GET /v1/doctors/{id}/slots?from=…&to=…
    API->>DB: SELECT WHERE status='available'
    DB-->>API: slot list
    API-->>P: {data: [slot1, slot2, …]}

    P->>API: POST /v1/bookings/hold\nIdempotency-Key: key-001\n{slotId}
    API->>DB: UPDATE slots SET status='held' WHERE id=… AND status='available' RETURNING *
    Note over DB: Row-level lock + EXCLUDE constraint
    DB-->>API: {slot, doctor, consultationFeeCents}
    API->>DB: INSERT consultations (status=pending_payment)
    DB-->>API: consultation row
    API-->>P: {holdId, slotId, heldUntil, doctor}

    P->>API: POST /v1/bookings/{holdId}/confirm\nIdempotency-Key: key-002\n{paymentMethodToken}
    API->>DB: UPDATE slots SET status='payment_pending'
    API->>GW: createIntent(amountCents, metadata)
    GW-->>API: {id: pi_mock_xxx, clientSecret}
    API->>DB: INSERT payments (status=initiated)
    API-->>P: {paymentId, providerRef, clientSecret, amountCents}

    GW->>API: POST /v1/payments/webhook\n{id: evt_xxx, type: payment.captured, data.object.id: pi_mock_xxx}
    Note over API: Verify HMAC-SHA256
    API->>DB: INSERT payment_events (providerEventId UNIQUE)
    API->>DB: UPDATE payments SET status=captured
    API->>DB: UPDATE slots SET status=booked
    API->>DB: UPDATE consultations SET status=scheduled
    API-->>GW: {processed: true}

    Note over P,GW: Consultation lifecycle

    P->>API: GET /v1/consultations/{id}
    API-->>P: {status: scheduled, scheduledStart, doctor}

    API->>API: Doctor logs in\nPOST /v1/consultations/{id}/start
    API->>DB: UPDATE consultations SET status=in_progress
    API-->>API: {status: in_progress, startedAt}

    API->>API: POST /v1/consultations/{id}/complete
    API->>DB: UPDATE consultations SET status=completed
    API-->>API: {status: completed, endedAt}

    API->>API: POST /v1/consultations/{id}/prescriptions\n{items: [{drugName,dosage,…}]}
    API->>DB: INSERT prescriptions (version=1, signedAt)
    API->>DB: INSERT prescription_items
    API-->>API: {id, version, items}

    Note over Q: Background — expired hold release

    Q->>DB: SELECT slots WHERE status IN (held,payment_pending) AND held_until < now()
    DB-->>Q: expired slots
    Q->>DB: UPDATE slots SET status=available; UPDATE consultations SET status=cancelled
